!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell line: A549
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = Cells were transduced with the Calabrese sgRNA library at an MOI of 0.5, then repeatedly infected with influenza B virus
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = A549 cells were maintained throughout the screen in DMEM supplemented with 10% FBS, Glutamax, and Pen/Strep
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = genomic DNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Surviving cells were collected, genomic DNA was extracted, and PCR for the sgRNA sequences was performed.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Illumina adaptors and barcodes were incorporated into the PCR primers. PCR amplified libraries were generated with independent barcodes to allow multiplexing.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = OTHER: CRISPR Screen
!Sample_description = Uninfected transduced library input (replicate 1)
!Sample_data_processing = The reads were mapped to the CRISPR Calabrese sgRNA library and raw reads for each sgRNA were counted using the MAGeCK pipeline
